{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And seven days were completed.</b> Scripture explained regarding the first plague, that of blood, that the plague lasted seven days, like the impurity of the menstruant (niddah): just as the impurity of the niddah is seven days, so too the plague of blood in Egypt was seven days. And Scripture revealed this regarding the plague of blood, which was the first, and the same reasoning applies to all the rest — each and every one lasted seven days, and the days of respite were twenty-one days, making a full month between the duration of the plague and the respite. And so we find that R. Eliezer ha-Kalir established in his piyyut and said: 'A month of days was apportioned for each plague — three parts appointed and waited, and the fourth the plague itself endured.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:56:54.191210718Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}